<title>USA: Converse says jury rules favorably on logo.</title>
<headline>Converse says jury rules favorably on logo.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH READING, Mass. 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A jury ruled that a proposed Starter Corp trademark would infringe upon Converse Corp's logo that it uses for its sneakers, Converse said on Friday.</p>
<p>Starter Corp was seeking a judgement against Converse in the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of New York, Converse said.</p>
<p>The jury found that Starter's proposed use of its S and star logo with the Starter name would infringe upon the converse five-pointed star trademark, Converse said.  </p>
<p>Converse said it began using the five-pointed star trademark in 1917 on its Chuck Taylor All Star line of basketball shoes. The company has sold 560 million pairs of the All Star sneaker worldwide.</p>
